<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Metamorphosis insectorum Surinamensium</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1705</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Metamorphosis insectorum Surinamensium is an illustrated book by the German-born naturalist and artist Maria Sibylla Merian, published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a> in 1705. Based on her stay in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a> from 1699 to 1701, its sixty plates show the life cycles of insects together with the plants they feed on. It became a landmark of natural history illustration and of the study of insect metamorphosis.</p></div>
